Chapter: BoundedFixedAccepted
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 Cost Model, the fixed rung, the arm that must COMPILE.
 `codex/test/errors/bounded-fixed-exceeded` proves the refusal; a refusal arm
 alone cannot tell a working check from one that refuses everything.

 `substring` is `budgeted:3` and argument 3 here is the literal 4, so the
 slice is the same 16 bytes whatever the line is. That is what `fixed`
 asserts and what `budgeted` does not require.

Section: A Width The Call Names

  bounded fixed field : Text -> Text
  field (line) = substring line 0 4

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni ("field=" & field "abcdefghij")
  end
